ifa/issues/146 E, via ifa/issues/133 -- under the start-merged default both comprehensions' `append` share one EntrySet because both accumulators ARE the merged list CreationSet, so route 4 cannot partition it ("1 group: every creation point on the same assign sets"). PYC_ESBLOCK=1 splits that EntrySet and fixes this fixture (tests/listcomp_element_separation_startmerged.py pins it, 0 warnings with the flag and 1 without), but ESBLOCK stays opt-in because it costs plcfrs and sudoku5 through 146 E's tuple-slot merge. Flips to PASS when 146 E lands and ESBLOCK can default on.
